349	/**
350	 * @brief   Copy data between source and destination buffers via EPIC device (supports frame buffer operations).
351	            Only in Render List Mode, if rotation is not 0(DRV_EPIC_ROT_NONE), the frame buffer will be rotated directly during the copy process.
352	 *          This function is used to copy a specific area of data from the source buffer to the destination buffer
353	 *          through the EPIC hardware device, and supports configuration of color formats and completion callbacks.
354	 * @param   src         Pointer to the source data buffer (uint8_t type), cannot be NULL
355	 * @param   dst         Pointer to the destination data buffer (uint8_t type), cannot be NULL
356	 * @param   src_area    Pointer to the source area definition structure (EPIC_AreaTypeDef),
357	 *                      specifies the position and size of the source buffer's valid area
358	 * @param   dst_area    Pointer to the destination area definition structure (EPIC_AreaTypeDef),
359	 *                      specifies the position and size of the destination buffer's valid area
360	 * @param   copy_area   Pointer to the copy area definition structure (EPIC_AreaTypeDef),
361	 *                      specifies the exact area (width/height/offset) to be copied from source to destination
362	 * @param   src_cf      Source buffer color format configuration (uint32_t type),
363	 * @param   dst_cf      Destination buffer color format configuration (uint32_t type),
364	 * @param   cbk         Pointer to the copy completion callback function (drv_epic_cplt_cbk),
365	 *                      this function will be called when the EPIC copy operation is finished;
